hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1107","Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala Al-San’ani told us, they said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Sa’id, h, and Bundar told us, And Yahya bin Hakim, and Al-Dawrqi, said: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, and Suleiman Al-Taymi, H, narrated to us Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani, Abdah told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, both of them on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, On the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two dawn prayers are better than the whole world,” and he said Al-Sana'ani in the two rak'ahs of Fajr: They are better than the whole world. In the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: “The two dawn rak’ahs are dearer to me than the whole world.” Muhammad bin Aslam told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, something similar to that."
